>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
## `register_quotient`

``` hol4
Refute.register_quotient :
  {qty : hol_type,
   rty : hol_type,
   abs : term,
   rep : term,
   equiv_thm : thm,
   partial : bool} -> unit
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Registers an existing quotient type with the model finder.

`qty` is the quotient type and `rty` its representation type.  `abs` and
`rep` must be existing constants of types `rty -> qty` and
`qty -> rty`.  `equiv_thm` must be a standard bare
`QUOTIENT equiv abs rep` theorem with no hypotheses.  This bridge theorem
is required because a total equivalence theorem alone does not establish
that arbitrary same-typed Abs/Rep constants implement its quotient.

The legacy `partial` record field is ignored: a verified `QUOTIENT` bridge
uses the sound partial encoding.

Registrations are session-local.  A valid later registration replaces the
same quotient type operator.  The model finder can also lazily harvest
standard quotient metadata; explicit registration is useful for a
nonstandard database location or shape.

### Failure

Fails for malformed parameter types, nonconstant or ill-typed Abs/Rep
terms, free or ill-typed equivalence relations, unsupported theorem
shapes, theorem hypotheses, a theorem naming different constants, or an
incompatible datatype, codatatype, typedef, or fraction classification.

### See also

[`Refute.register_typedef`](#Refute.register_typedef),
[`Refute.register_codatatype`](#Refute.register_codatatype),
[`Refute.register_frac_type`](#Refute.register_frac_type),
[`Refute.nitpick`](#Refute.nitpick)

Quotient encoding is described in \ref{Description:the-holrefute-library}.
